*  POKER_driver - drives poker.spt, which plays cold-hand five-card poker
*  between two players with nothing wild, and with it the ABCDR, ALPHA, BETA
*  and BET functions the manifest names for this module.  Contract per
*  poker.spt header.  POKER carries its own END, so a driver can only be the
*  include plus scripted answers on stdin.  The form's INPUT(.INPUT,5,
*  'phrases.in') finds phrases.in under its lower-case name, and the program
*  then re-opens INPUT on ' -f0' and plays a whole game on standard input:
*  poker_driver.input's answers run out and sbl -bf asks again forever
*  (OUTSIDE_SPITBOL_BASELINE.tsv).  Owed: an input that plays the game to its
*  end (UNGRADED.tsv, NEEDS_STDIN_FIXTURE).
-INCLUDE "poker.spt"
